# Probability cycles (A:B): SELECT on a held step, down past 5%: 1:2 2:2 1:3 ... 8:8. A step at A:B plays on
# the A-th of every B passes of its part's pattern. A kick on 1, 5, 9, 13; step 1 at 1:4 (passes 1 and 5 of
# 8), step 9 at 2:2 (passes 2, 4, 6, 8): with NOTES OUT, 2 + 8 + 4 + 8 = 22 kicks in 8 bars.
wait 300
tapkey b0
tapkey w0
tapkey w4
tapkey w8
tapkey w12
# 100 % is position 0; 5 % is 19; then 1:2 (20), 2:2 (21), 1:3, 2:3, 3:3, 1:4 (25)
key w0 down
turn SELECT -25
key w0 up
expect laneval7.0.0.0 106
key w8 down
turn SELECT -21
key w8 up
expect laneval7.0.0.8 102
# the end of the line: 8:8, and back up to 100 % (no value)
key w12 down
turn SELECT -60
key w12 up
expect laneval7.0.0.12 135
key w12 down
turn SELECT 60
key w12 up
expect laneval7.0.0.12 255
expect hit0.0.0 1
expect hit0.0.8 1
tap GLO
turn SELECT 1
turn ALGO 1
tap HOME
tap EDIT
expect noteons 0
tap PLAY
wait 15000
tap PLAY
expect noteons 22
